---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ConcreteCalculator from '../../components/ConcreteCalculator.astro';
import { webApplicationSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/schema';
import { CALCULATORS_HUB } from '../../data/tools';

const path = '/calculators/concrete-calculator';
const title = 'Concrete Calculator: Cubic Yards & Bag Calculator';
const description =
  'Estimate how much concrete you need in cubic yards, cubic feet, and bags. Calculate slabs, circular pads, and post holes with adjustable extra material.';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: CALCULATORS_HUB.title, href: '/calculators' },
  { label: 'Concrete Calculator' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  schema={[
    webApplicationSchema({
      name: 'Concrete Calculator',
      description,
      path,
    }),
    breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  ]}
>
  <div class="container-site section-space">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

    <header class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="section-heading">Concrete Calculator</h1>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Estimate concrete volume in cubic yards and cubic feet, then see how many bags to buy for slabs,
        circular pads, and post holes. Enter your own dimensions — this tool does not choose thickness or
        footing size for you.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <ConcreteCalculator />
    </div>

    <p class="concrete-page__disclaimer mt-8 max-w-3xl">
      This calculator estimates concrete volume and bag counts from the dimensions you enter. It does not
      determine slab thickness, footing size, concrete strength (PSI), reinforcement, structural suitability,
      or building-code compliance. Confirm bag yields on the product you buy and follow local codes and
      manufacturer instructions.
    </p>

    <article class="prose-article concrete-page__copy mt-14 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>How the concrete calculation works</h2>
      <p>
        The calculator converts your dimensions to feet, then computes volume in cubic feet. Rectangular
        projects use length × width × thickness. Circular pads and post holes use the cylinder formula
        π × radius² × depth. Cubic yards are cubic feet ÷ 27. Extra material is applied as a percentage on
        top of that calculated volume. Bag counts divide the purchase volume by each bag’s approximate yield
        and round <strong>up</strong> to whole bags.
      </p>

      <h2>Concrete bag yields</h2>
      <p>
        Bag counts in the results use approximate yields published for QUIKRETE Concrete Mix #1101:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>40 lb ≈ 0.30 ft³</li>
        <li>50 lb ≈ 0.375 ft³</li>
        <li>60 lb ≈ 0.45 ft³</li>
        <li>80 lb ≈ 0.60 ft³</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Other concrete products can yield differently. Always confirm the yield printed on the bag you purchase.
      </p>

      <h2>How much extra concrete should you plan for?</h2>
      <p>
        Ready-mix industry guidance from the National Ready Mixed Concrete Association discusses ordering
        about 4–10% more than a plan-dimension estimate to cover contingencies such as waste and
        over-excavation. Sakrete’s calculator guidance recommends adding about 10% when estimating bagged
        jobs. This tool defaults to 10% as an editable estimating assumption — not a requirement. You can
        set 0%, 5%, 10%, or a custom value up to 25%.
      </p>

      <h2>Bags vs ready-mix</h2>
      <p>
        Compare the cubic-yard estimate with the bag counts. Larger pours are often ordered as ready-mix.
        Local suppliers may have minimum orders and delivery fees. This calculator does not set a universal
        cutoff between bags and a truck.
      </p>

      <h2>Example calculations</h2>
      <h3>10 × 10 ft slab, 4 in thick, 10% extra</h3>
      <p>
        Calculated volume ≈ 1.23 yd³ (33.33 ft³). With 10% extra ≈ 1.36 yd³. About 62 of the 80 lb bags using
        the #1101 yield table.
      </p>
      <h3>12 × 16 ft slab, 4 in thick, 10% extra</h3>
      <p>
        Calculated volume ≈ 2.37 yd³ (64 ft³). With 10% extra ≈ 2.61 yd³. About 118 of the 80 lb bags.
      </p>
      <h3>Four post holes, 12 in diameter × 36 in deep, 10% extra</h3>
      <p>
        Full cylindrical hole volume ≈ 0.35 yd³ before extra. With 10% extra, about 18 of the 80 lb bags.
        Post volume is not subtracted.
      </p>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>How do I calculate cubic yards of concrete?</h3>
      <p>
        Convert all dimensions to feet, multiply to get cubic feet, then divide by 27. This calculator does
        that conversion for you and also shows cubic meters.
      </p>
      <h3>How many 80 lb bags are in one cubic yard?</h3>
      <p>
        Using the 0.60 ft³ approximate yield for an 80 lb QUIKRETE Concrete Mix bag, one cubic yard is about
        45 bags before extra material (27 ÷ 0.60).
      </p>
      <h3>Should I add extra concrete?</h3>
      <p>
        Many estimators add a contingency for uneven subgrade, spillage, and measurement variance. Industry
        ready-mix guidance often cites a 4–10% range. Use the control that matches your situation, or 0% if
        you only want the raw geometric volume.
      </p>
      <h3>Can I use this calculator for post holes?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Choose Post holes, enter hole diameter, depth, and count. Results use the full cylinder volume
        and do not subtract the post.
      </p>
      <h3>Does this calculator tell me how thick a slab should be?</h3>
      <p>
        No. You enter the thickness you already plan to use. Thickness, reinforcement, and strength selection
        are outside the scope of this quantity tool.
      </p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.quikrete.com/pdfs/data_sheet-concrete%20mix%201101.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            QUIKRETE Concrete Mix #1101 data sheet
          </a>
          — approximate bag yields
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.nrmca.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/31pr.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            NRMCA CIP 31 — Ordering Ready Mixed Concrete
          </a>
          — 4–10% contingency guidance when ordering ready-mix
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.sakrete.com/concrete-calculators/" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Sakrete Concrete Calculators
          </a>
          — manufacturer estimating tip to add about 10%
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .concrete-page__disclaimer {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .concrete-page__copy {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .concrete-page__copy :where(h2, h3) {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
